      "locked": false,
      "text": "Low level design crack: \n\nNote: \n    What we are not going to discuss here\n\n1. DSA/OA/Problem solving coding questions\n    -> focus of these to solve in most optimised way , not need to be in oops format\n        using datastructure and algorithm, not related to real world system .\n\n2. High level design \n    -> here expentation to draw the high level and its working/nfr -> here also we discuss\n        about apis design and data model design but not class or machine coding. \n\n\n\nFocus of this template -> three category: \n\n1. oops + dsa:\n    -> problem where require to solve including design pattern and oops \n    -> but not very high scope.\n    -> here you'll have to create 3-4 classes only -> no service type structure etc. \n    -> basically good problem solving as well as normal oops with repo structure\n        for e.g. LFU, LRU etc. \n    -> not need of dbschema, api design, class diagram etc. just need to use oops, design pattern etc. \n    -> language -> dsa + oops \n    -> golang might fail here. since focus still on problem solving , time complexity etc. \n\nE.g. -> rippling, joveo etc. \n\n\n2. Machine coding: \n    -> Requirements will be given similar to high level design\n    -> like uber design, parking lot, booking , etc. \n    -> Assume it has like you need to create the monolith service for these requirements. \n    -> expectation -> write production ready code + design pattern + models + module + running etc .\n    -> without route or api -> some time like sharechat can ask for api as well. \n\nE.g. phonepe, flipkart, sharechat, swiggy etc. \n\n\n3. LLd ( without coding ) \n    -> Requirements will be given similar to high level design\n    -> like uber design, parking lot, booking , etc. \n    -> focus here \n    -> understand the requirements. \n    -> DB Schema designing. \n    -> Api designing. \n    -> Class diagram designing.\n\nbasically tell how this backend service code will be written. ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Low level design crack: \n\nNote: \n    What we are not going to discuss here\n\n1. DSA/OA/Problem solving coding questions\n    -> focus of these to solve in most optimised way , not need to be in oops format\n        using datastructure and algorithm, not related to real world system .\n\n2. High level design \n    -> here expentation to draw the high level and its working/nfr -> here also we discuss\n        about apis design and data model design but not class or machine coding. \n\n\n\nFocus of this template -> three category: \n\n1. oops + dsa:\n    -> problem where require to solve including design pattern and oops \n    -> but not very high scope.\n    -> here you'll have to create 3-4 classes only -> no service type structure etc. \n    -> basically good problem solving as well as normal oops with repo structure\n        for e.g. LFU, LRU etc. \n    -> not need of dbschema, api design, class diagram etc. just need to use oops, design pattern etc. \n    -> language -> dsa + oops \n    -> golang might fail here. since focus still on problem solving , time complexity etc. \n\nE.g. -> rippling, joveo etc. \n\n\n2. Machine coding: \n    -> Requirements will be given similar to high level design\n    -> like uber design, parking lot, booking , etc. \n    -> Assume it has like you need to create the monolith service for these requirements. \n    -> expectation -> write production ready code + design pattern + models + module + running etc .\n    -> without route or api -> some time like sharechat can ask for api as well. \n\nE.g. phonepe, flipkart, sharechat, swiggy etc. \n\n\n3. LLd ( without coding ) \n    -> Requirements will be given similar to high level design\n    -> like uber design, parking lot, booking , etc. \n    -> focus here \n    -> understand the requirements. \n    -> DB Schema designing. \n    -> Api designing. \n    -> Class diagram designing.\n\nbasically tell how this backend service code will be written. ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
