      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1766661627645,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "-> How much time uptil now ? (15min, will back on this ) \n\n-Note make sure, write less attribute but write properly , also write name properly\n not like childish.\n- if this this. machine coding write all these in model folders.  ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "-> How much time uptil now ? (15min, will back on this ) \n\n-Note make sure, write less attribute but write properly , also write name properly\n not like childish.\n- if this this. machine coding write all these in model folders.  ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "dtyeOwKoH0T0_dXOdBTZO",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4979.617316250553,
      "y": 1162.629617624345,
      "width": 862.0194702148438,
      "height": 675,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#9c36b5",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "af",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 595573227,
      "version": 1407,
      "versionNonce": 561043691,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1766662472322,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "......\n\n-> Once we are done with this. \n-> create the service layers\n-> tell interviewer, we do also have controller layer -> that do request validation -> but \n    as of now ignoring that considering the time, if we have more time\n    i'll write that.\n-> write the one by one \n    -> write the method.\n    -> now problematic part here is the method attributes\n    -> for dao we have models so its ok\n    -> but for service ? \n        -> so we have two ways here.\n            -> either create dto or require which are kind of club of different models.\n                or it can be simpler as per require and take single argument for service. \n            -> or take it as normal multiple types \n\n            -> it its too many arguments, better to have dto/request model \n            -> if few like 3-4 , better we can take as normal types and can tell \n                to interview ideally these should be request model, but due to time \n                contrainst didn't write this.\n\n-> after this or before this write dao in service attributes.\n-> Now write the dao as correxponding to models.\n        -> user hashmap to store in inmemory.\n        -> usually need simple crud methods only.  \n            ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "......\n\n-> Once we are done with this. \n-> create the service layers\n-> tell interviewer, we do also have controller layer -> that do request validation -> but \n    as of now ignoring that considering the time, if we have more time\n    i'll write that.\n-> write the one by one \n    -> write the method.\n    -> now problematic part here is the method attributes\n    -> for dao we have models so its ok\n    -> but for service ? \n        -> so we have two ways here.\n            -> either create dto or require which are kind of club of different models.\n                or it can be simpler as per require and take single argument for service. \n            -> or take it as normal multiple types \n\n            -> it its too many arguments, better to have dto/request model \n            -> if few like 3-4 , better we can take as normal types and can tell \n                to interview ideally these should be request model, but due to time \n                contrainst didn't write this.\n\n-> after this or before this write dao in service attributes.\n-> Now write the dao as correxponding to models.\n        -> user hashmap to store in inmemory.\n        -> usually need simple crud methods only.  \n            ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
